Exercise 04: midLS
Turn-in directory: ex04/
Files to turn in: midLS
Allowed functions: None
In a file named midLS, write the command that lists all files and directories in your
current directory (excluding hidden files or any file starting with a dot, including
double dots).
• The output should be sorted by modification date, with entries separated by a
comma and a space.
• Directory names should end with a slash (/).

**************
So there are few commands in the family of ls:
ls: show all NOT HIDDEN files, by default
ls -a: show all files, including hidden ones
ls -A: show all hidden files
ls -p: show / after the directory name
  here the p means path/pathname indicator
ls -t: order by time, from newest to oldest
ls -r: order by time, but reverse, from oldest to newest
ls -m: with entries separated by acomma and a space.
  here m means stmream format

and with bash command, we can check it.
bash: 
  bash: only bash means open a new subshell
  bash + file name: read and execute the file or script

then do the git push regularly.

